# 1. What Is a Deployment Strategy?

A Deployment controls application Pods.

```text
Deployment
    ↓
ReplicaSet
    ↓
Pods
```

When an application version changes, OpenShift needs to decide:

> How should the old Pods be replaced?

This behavior is controlled by the **Deployment strategy**.

The two strategies we will practice:

```text
RollingUpdate
Recreate
```

---

# 2. RollingUpdate

RollingUpdate replaces old Pods gradually with new Pods.

Conceptually:

```text
Old Version
    Pod A
    Pod B
    Pod C
       ↓
New Version
    Pod A
    Pod B
    Pod C
```

During the rollout, old and new versions can temporarily exist together.

```text
v1 → Pod A
v1 → Pod B
v2 → Pod D

       ↓

v1 → Pod B
v2 → Pod D
v2 → Pod E

       ↓

v2 → Pod D
v2 → Pod E
v2 → Pod F
```

This normally provides minimal application disruption.

