# 3. OpenShift and nginx Permission Issue

During this lesson, using:

```text
nginx:1.25
```

with the default nginx configuration caused:

```text
CrashLoopBackOff
```

The important error was:

```text
mkdir() "/var/cache/nginx/client_temp" failed (13: Permission denied)
```

We also saw:

```text
sed: couldn't open temporary file /etc/nginx/... Permission denied
```

### Root Cause

OpenShift runs containers under restricted/non-root security settings.

The standard nginx configuration expects to write to locations such as:

```text
/var/cache/nginx
/etc/nginx
```

which are not writable by the restricted runtime user.

Therefore, for this lesson we use:

```text
ConfigMap
    ↓
Custom nginx.conf
    ↓
Listen on 8080
    ↓
Temporary files → /tmp
    ↓
Logs → stdout/stderr
```

This allows us to focus on the Deployment strategies instead of repeatedly troubleshooting nginx permissions.

