# 14. Recreate Strategy

The second strategy is:

```text
Recreate
```

Recreate works differently from RollingUpdate.

Conceptually:

```text
Old Pods
    ↓
Deleted
    ↓
No application Pods
    ↓
New Pods created
```

Example:

```text
v1 → Pod A
v1 → Pod B
v1 → Pod C

       ↓

DELETE

       ↓

No Pods

       ↓

v2 → Pod A
v2 → Pod B
v2 → Pod C
```

This can cause application downtime.

---

# 15. Recreate – OpenShift-Compatible YAML

Create:

```text
lesson18-recreate.yaml
```

Use:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: lesson18-recreate-nginx-config
data:
  nginx.conf: |
    worker_processes auto;
    pid /tmp/nginx.pid;

    events {
      worker_connections 1024;
    }

    http {
      access_log /dev/stdout;
      error_log /dev/stderr;

      client_body_temp_path /tmp/client_temp;
      proxy_temp_path /tmp/proxy_temp;
      fastcgi_temp_path /tmp/fastcgi_temp;
      uwsgi_temp_path /tmp/uwsgi_temp;
      scgi_temp_path /tmp/scgi_temp;

      server {
        listen 8080;
        server_name _;

        location / {
          root /usr/share/nginx/html;
          index index.html;
        }
      }
    }

---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: lesson18-recreate
spec:
  replicas: 3
  strategy:
    type: Recreate
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: lesson18-recreate
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: lesson18-recreate
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: web
          image: nginx:1.25
          command:
            - nginx
            - -c
            - /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
            - -g
            - daemon off;
          ports:
            - containerPort: 8080
          volumeMounts:
            - name: nginx-config
              mountPath: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
              subPath: nginx.conf
            - name: nginx-tmp
              mountPath: /tmp
      volumes:
        - name: nginx-config
          configMap:
            name: lesson18-recreate-nginx-config
        - name: nginx-tmp
          emptyDir: {}
```

