# 19. RollingUpdate vs Recreate

| Strategy | Behavior | Downtime |
|---|---|---|
| RollingUpdate | Gradually replaces Pods | Usually minimal/no downtime |
| Recreate | Deletes old Pods before creating new Pods | Possible downtime |

Easy memory:

```text
RollingUpdate

Old → New gradually
```

```text
Recreate

Old → Delete → New
```

---

# 20. Why Use Recreate?

Recreate can be useful when:

- Old and new versions cannot run simultaneously
- The application requires a clean restart
- Old and new versions conflict with shared resources
- Temporary downtime is acceptable

For most normal web applications:

```text
RollingUpdate
```

is generally preferred.

