# 21. Blue/Green Deployment

Blue/Green keeps two application versions.

```text
Blue
 ↓
Version 1

Green
 ↓
Version 2
```

Example:

```text
             Service
                |
                v
             Blue v1
```

Deploy v2 separately:

```text
             Service
                |
                v
             Blue v1

             Green v2
```

After testing Green, traffic can be switched:

```text
             Service
                |
                v
             Green v2
```

### Remember

```text
Blue = Old Version

Green = New Version
```

For now, learn Blue/Green as a concept. We can build a complete implementation later.

---

# 22. Canary Deployment

Canary sends only a small amount of traffic to the new version.

Example:

```text
Users
  |
  +---- 90% → v1
  |
  +---- 10% → v2
```

If v2 works:

```text
50% → v1
50% → v2
```

Eventually:

```text
100% → v2
```

The purpose is to reduce deployment risk.

---

# 23. Deployment Strategy Comparison

```text
RollingUpdate
    ↓
Gradually replace Pods
```

```text
Recreate
    ↓
Delete old Pods
    ↓
Create new Pods
```

```text
Blue/Green
    ↓
Run two versions
    ↓
Switch traffic
```

```text
Canary
    ↓
Small percentage of traffic
    ↓
Test new version
    ↓
Gradually increase traffic
```

