# 28. Important Lesson Learned From nginx

During this lesson, we initially used:

```text
nginx:1.25
```

with the default configuration.

It failed because:

```text
/var/cache/nginx
```

was not writable under the OpenShift restricted/non-root runtime.

The error was:

```text
mkdir() "/var/cache/nginx/client_temp" failed (13: Permission denied)
```

We also attempted to modify:

```text
/etc/nginx/nginx.conf
```

at runtime and received:

```text
Permission denied
```

### Correct approach

Instead of modifying protected files at startup:

```text
❌ sed /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
❌ write /var/cache/nginx
```

we use:

```text
ConfigMap
    ↓
Custom nginx.conf
    ↓
Port 8080
    ↓
/tmp for temporary files
    ↓
stdout/stderr for logs
```

This is a useful OpenShift security lesson.

